  "transpose": false,
  "notes": "Target requires blending pre-retirement and post-retirement mortality rates. The document provides explicit sample rates for Pre-Retirement (Table on page 69) but only describes the Post-Retirement tables (RP-2014 Healthy Annuitant) on page 68 without printing sample rates. Therefore, the 'group_weighted' operation can only utilize the Pre-Retirement rates (Male/Female) weighted by the Active Member counts (Table 3). Post-retirement rates are excluded from the calculation due to lack of numerical data in the document. The resulting column represents the unisex pre-retirement mortality probability. Target ages 70-119 have no source data as the Pre-Retirement table ends at age 69 (span 65-69). The '70 & over' active member bin (Table 3) is clipped to [70, 119] for weight purposes, but since there are no rates for these ages, the weights are effectively unused for the rate calculation. Values are printed as percentages (e.g., 0.05) and converted to decimal probabilities.",
  "unavailable": false,
  "broadcast": null
}